  "question": {
    "text": "At STP, 2.8 litres of hydrogen sulphide were mixed with 1.6 litres of sulphur dioxide and the reaction occurred according to the equation<br />\r<math><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\rWhich of the following shows the volume of the gas remaining after the reaction?"
  },
